  "distance_km": 10.6,
  "description": "This walk follows a section of the South West Coast Path from Burton Bradstock to Abbotsbury. The route runs for 6.6 miles along a fairly flat trail. You can start off from the car park at Burton Beach and then head south east, passing the pretty Burton Mere and the village of West Bexington. The final section leaves the coast and climbs towards Abbotsbury, passing the lovely Abbotsbury Subtropical Gardens and the historic Abbotsbury Castle before finishing in the village. There's splendid coastal views throughout and the option of extending your walk along the famous Chesil Beach towards Weymouth.",
